# Program: mloc v10.5.0, release date 4/10/2020
# Run: illapel8.28
# Author: EBergman
# Date: 20200511 140148.206
#                                                                                                                        
# The Illapel cluster is named for the city of Illapel in Choapa Province,
# Coquimbo Region, Chile. The cluster is based on the 8.3 Mw earthquake of
# September 16, 2015, but it includes both earlier and more recent events.
# In addition to the M8.3 Illapel event, the cluster contains an M7.2
# aftershock and 9 events with M6.0-6.9. The cluster is mainly composed of
# events on-shore, to maintain good azimuthal coverage and depth control.
# All events have depth control from near-source or local-distance
# readings and many events also have strong constraint on depth from
# telelseismic depth phases. The agreement between the two methods is
# quite good, and the fit of arrival times for events both above and below
# the Moho to the theoretical times calculated from the 1-D crustal model
# used for local and regional travel-time calculations is also quite good.
#                                                                                                                        
# Number of events:  54
# Calibration type: direct calibration using data to  1.0 degrees; hypocentroid calibration level =  1.4 km
# Epicentral calibration range:  2 -  4 km
# Date range: 20010101 - 20191104
# Latitude range: -31.994 - -30.969
# Longitude range:  -71.837 -  -71.111
# Depth range:  18.0 -  73.0
# Magnitude range: 3.6 - 8.3
